# act (nektos/act) default flags for local CI iteration.
#
# Usage: invoke `act` (or via tools/act-cell) from repo root; act reads
# this file automatically. See AGENTS.md §3.6 "Local CI iteration with
# act" for the operator-facing workflow.

# Runner images — catthehacker's "js" variants are the smallest images
# that include Node.js (and the surrounding GHA action toolchain), which
# is required by stock JS-based actions like actions/cache@v4 and
# actions/checkout@v4. The slim "act-*" variants do NOT ship node and
# cause `actions/cache@v4` to fail with `node: executable file not found`
# (see push-18 cache validation run).
#
# The "full-*" variants (~60GB extracted) also include node + gh, and
# tools/momus-local pins itself to `full-latest` because the reusable
# momus workflow shells out to `gh`. For per-cell CI iteration we don't
# need `gh`, so `js-*` is the right balance of size vs functionality.
-P ubuntu-latest=catthehacker/ubuntu:js-latest
-P ubuntu-22.04=catthehacker/ubuntu:js-22.04
-P ubuntu-24.04=catthehacker/ubuntu:js-24.04

# Force linux/amd64 even on Apple Silicon. Most GitHub Actions
# (setup-nim-action, actions/cache@v4) only ship amd64 binaries; arm64
# emulation via Docker Desktop's qemu is slow (3-5x) but correct.
--container-architecture linux/amd64

# Reuse containers across runs of the same job so dep installs cache.
# Combine with `--rm` on the CLI if you want a clean slate.
--reuse

# Pull images on first reference, then leave alone. Avoids re-pulling
# the ~2GB catthehacker image on every invocation.
--pull=false

# Persistent artifact/cache servers so actions/cache@v4 hits across act
# runs. Both directories live under ~/.cache/act and survive between
# invocations; the operator (or wrapper) handles cleanup. See AGENTS.md
# §3.6 "Caching" subsection.
--artifact-server-path /Users/eek/.cache/act/artifacts
--cache-server-path /Users/eek/.cache/act/cache
